      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "$$\n¬(Y∧X)⇔Y≡[¬(Y∧X)⇒Y]∧\n$$\n\nWhat expression should be inserted into the blank space above to give logically equivalent statements?",
      "worked_solution": "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $A⇔B$ is true if $A⇒B$ **and** $B⇒A.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $A⇔B$ is true if $A$ and $B$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nSo, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n¬(Y∧X)⇔Y≡[¬(Y∧X)⇒Y]∧[\\,Y⇒¬(Y∧X)].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing part is $Y⇒¬(Y∧X).$",
